{"id":96239869084285,"type":"artist","name":"Scott Walker","artist":null,"year":1943,"weight":42,"info":{"tags":["singer-songwriter","experimental","Avant-Garde","baroque pop","pop"],"country":"GB","begin":"1943-01-09","end":"2019-03-22","kind":"Person","similar":["The Walker Brothers","John Cale","Tom Waits","David Sylvian","Tim Buckley","Nico","This Heat","Van Dyke Parks","Scott Walker + Sunn O)))","The Angels of Light"],"disambiguation":"singer‐songwriter, musician and producer","img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Fenklup1968ScottWalker.jpg?width=500","bio":"Scott Walker (9 de enero de 1943 - 24 de marzo de 2019) fue un brillante cantante/compositor americano dado a recluirse que ha vivido en Inglaterra durante los últimos 40 años. Noel Scott Engel, su nombre real, tuvo una efímera carrera en EE.UU. en su adolescencia antes de irse a Inglaterra en 1965 para librarse del servicio militar. Como líder de los llamados Walker Brothers (no eran hermanos), se convirtió en una estrella de la invasión británica."},"works":[{"id":79909697620624,"type":"album","name":"Scott","artist":"Scott Walker","year":1967,"weight":5,"yt":"-RR3GVNK0cs","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":35507544569942,"name":"RYM Top — Pop — Baroque Pop","rank":67,"scaruffi":null},{"id":135407159101775,"name":"RYM Top — Pop — Traditional Pop","rank":58,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":2}},{"id":244354624839033,"type":"album","name":"Scott 2","artist":"Scott Walker","year":1968,"weight":8,"yt":"8n5FLWAjcSQ","src":"charts,musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":192934750972716,"name":"1001 Albums You Must Hear Before You Die","rank":130,"scaruffi":null},{"id":35507544569942,"name":"RYM Top — Pop — Baroque Pop","rank":63,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":2}},{"id":13443190113765,"type":"album","name":"Scott 3","artist":"Scott Walker","year":1969,"weight":8,"yt":"W5GO49AsWHo","src":"charts,musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":1