al) pasó factura: crisis y hospitalizaciones (Jagger en junio, el aparente intento de suicidio de Scott Walker en agosto), Brian Jones desaparecido, Paul Jones dejó Manfred Mann, los Animals se rehicieron como New Animals, Georgie Fame disolvió los Blue Flames. La novela All Night Stand de Thom Keyes, un roman à clef sobre los Beatles, acaba con su estrella aburrida de sí misma. Sin el centro unificador de los Beatles volvió el entretenimiento ligero (los Bachelors, Ken Dodd y «Distant Drums» del difunto Jim Reeves, número 1 casi todo octubre), mientras en agosto la mitad del Top 50 británico era americana: Motown y los grupos de la Costa Oeste. «Una era ha terminado», escribió Chris Welch.","color":"#ef4444","family":"Beat británico, mod y freakbeat","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/#fin-del-beat"},{"id":243962098886055,"name":"Carreras en solitario: cantautores de finales de los sesenta","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1967,"end":1972,"desc":"Los excéntricos de Los Ángeles (David Axelrod, cuyos breakbeats orquestales anticipan el trip-hop; Van Dyke Parks y su música de cámara pop; David Ackles, Kim Fowley, Wild Man Fischer) y los herederos del Greenwich (Laura Nyro, Eric Andersen, David Peel, Angus MacLise y Nico, cuyas letanías fúnebres inventan el rock gótico casi por accidente: Marble Index, Desert Shore). Canadá aporta a Leonard Cohen, Gordon Lightfoot, Joni Mitchell (Blue, Hejira) y Neil Young, que con Dylan y Springsteen forma la gran tríada «moral» de la música americana e inventa la guitarra distorsionada que influirá en el grunge. En Texas, Townes Van Zandt; en Gran Bretaña, Scott Walker, Nick Drake (Pink Moon), Roy Harper, John Martyn, Cat Stevens, Rod Stewart, Eric Burdon y Jack Bruce.","color":"#a3e635","family":"Folk y cantautores","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#solo-60s"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":121791170731970,"artist":"Scott Walker","artist_id":96239869084285,"title":"Scott 4","year":1969,"ess":1,"yt":"D4AU-Q2iZW4","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Carreras en solitario: cantautores de finales de los sesenta","scene_id":243962098886055,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#solo-60s","chapters":["Sección 3.3"],"pages":[[1,54,null]]},{"id":263183145628851,"artist":"Scott Walker","artist_id":96239869084285,"title":"Climate of Hunter","year":1984,"ess":0,"yt":"KXrnuBJnYZ0","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Carreras en solitario: cantautores de finales de los sesenta","scene_id":243962098886055,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#solo-60s","chapters":["Sección 3.3"],"pages":[[1,54,null]]},{"id":61948265170210,"artist":"Scott Walker","artist_id":96239869084285,"title":"Tilt","year":1995,"ess":0,"yt":"A93iAGO5fto","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Carreras en solitario: cantautores de finales de los sesenta","scene_id":243962098886055,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#solo-60s","chapters":["Sección 3.3"],"pages":[[1,54,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":54,"text":"…for harmonium, bass and percussion, and Dandruff (Virgin, 1974), a collection of 45 pieces for harmonium, do not quite fit in any category. In 1967 Scott Walker (2), who had been a pop star a` la Beatles (radio-friendly refrains for mass consumption, a marketing campaign focused on his cute looks), began…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Influence on Suede","body":"Scott Walker was mentioned as a significant influence on Suede, contributing to their distinct \"glam\" and \"intellectual\" musical style, alongside David Bowie. \"Suede que era como muy influenciada como David Bowie o Scott Walker.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"OASIS: Pilares del Brit Pop","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hHuqc4TgoOs"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Jarvis Cocker's Artistic Influence","body":"Scott Walker's work deeply influenced Jarvis Cocker, particularly in Pulp's later career. Cocker \"deepened\" his interest in Walker's charismatic classics, which ultimately led him to develop a \"modern experimental\" singing style and move completely away from the Brit-Pop sound. \"Jarvis Cocker began to work in a totally different way, delving into that stage that he had liked so much at the beginning of being Scott Walker of those great charismatic classics.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"PULP: Pilares del Brit Pop","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0r8_s6hR3Ss"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Musical Comparison","body":"Mickey Baker's version of J.B. Lenoir's \"Alabama Blues\" (retitled \"Alabama March\"), which incorporated string techniques learned from Iannis Xenakis, ended up sounding \"like nothing as much as Scott Walker.\" \"Like in this version of J. B. Linus, Alabama Blues, Revitant as Alabama March, which ends up sounding like nothing as much as Scott Walker.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"A History of Rock Music in 500 Songs","episode":"Episode 49: \"Love is Strange\" by Mickey and Sylvia","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FkyLPVvPbcI"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":79909697620624,"type":"album","name":"Scott","list_id":35507544569942,"list":"RYM Top — Pop — Baroque Pop","src":"musthear","rank":67,"year":1967,"note":null,"yt":"-RR3GVNK0cs","scaruffi":null},{"id":79909697620624,"type":"album","name":"Scott","list_id":135407159101775,"list":"RYM Top — Pop — Traditional Pop","src":"musthear","rank":58,"year":1967,"note":null,"yt":"-RR3GVNK0cs","scaruffi":null},{"id"